# Go Coding Standards

## Code Style
- Follow Go formatting standards (use `gofmt` or `go fmt`)
- Use meaningful variable and function names
- Keep functions focused and concise
- Use proper error handling with explicit error returns

## Package Structure
- Use the `dbconnect` package for main functionality
- Follow Go package naming conventions
- Keep packages focused on specific functionality

## Error Handling
- Use the custom error types defined in [dbconnect/errors.go](mdc:dbconnect/errors.go)
- Wrap errors with context using `WithType()` function
- Always check and handle errors explicitly
- Use `errors.Is()` for error type checking

## Authentication
- Follow the patterns established in [dbconnect/auth.go](mdc:dbconnect/auth.go)
- Use the unified auth credentials for Databricks authentication
- Implement proper gRPC credential interfaces

## Testing
- Write tests for all public functions
- Use the test patterns shown in the Makefile
- Run tests with `make test` command
